From 83d844d54d3938827b0cc182a6fe37f82346aa97 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 16:15:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 121/121] i2c: mediatek: require exact Curie board control

The first bounded Fermi run stopped at the D3 comparator after receiving
0x1f through a transport-valid native FIFO transaction. The low-bit 0x05
predicate came from an over-specific reading of BUCK_CONF.

The legacy datasheet defines raw PHASE_SEL_A values above 01 as
DA9213-only encodings whose effective phase count is limited to two on
DA9214. The observed 0x1f is therefore compatible with the DA9214 control
state on this board, but it is neither a unique semiconductor identity nor
a topology fingerprint.

Replace Fermi with the compile-time-exclusive Curie successor. Require
the complete D3 byte to equal the already observed 0x1f on both passes,
describe it as exact board control, and retain full-byte pass-to-pass
stability.

Keep the Fermi transfer order, receive prefills, native packed FIFO path,
zero-APDMA contract, counters, early-stop behavior, and stability checks
unchanged.

